{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-11-07T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A volcano, a rainforest and a bamboo grove? Haleakalā National Park on Maui has all three. Spanning Maui from its 3,055-metre summit to the coast, the park protects landscapes that change dramatically with elevation, rainfall and temperature. It was established in 1916 as part of Hawaii National Park and became its own national park in 1961. The name Haleakalā translates to 'House of the Sun', reflecting the Hawaiian mo'olelo of Māui capturing the sun to lengthen the day.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_ROW7076353112_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.PipiwaiTrail_ROW7076353112_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Bamboo forest, Pīpīwai Trail, Haleakalā National Park, Maui, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© MNStudio/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Haleakala+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261106_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261106_PipiwaiTrail"},"Ssd":"20261106","Name":"PipiwaiTrail","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7076353112","FullDateString":"6 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"A simple wooden stile leads into one of England's most celebrated landscapes. The Lake District, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, is a patchwork of shimmering lakes, rugged fells and centuries-old stone walls, all shaped by both nature and farming traditions.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.StileCrossing_ROW6996983847_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.StileCrossing_ROW6996983847_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Wooden stile at a stone wall, Black Crag, Lake District, England","Copyright":"© Alex Treadway/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261105_StileCrossing\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+District&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261105_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261105_StileCrossing"},"Ssd":"20261105","Name":"StileCrossing","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6996983847","FullDateString":"5 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"People paddle through a glowing maze of bald cypress in Xuancheng, Anhui, where autumn transforms flooded woodlands into a tapestry of amber, copper and deep rust. Known scientifically as 'Taxodium distichum', bald cypress is unusual among conifers because it sheds its soft, feathery needles each fall, turning reddish-brown before they drop.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_ROW6919148725_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AutumnChina_ROW6919148725_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"People rowing among colourful bald cypress, Xuancheng, Anhui, China","Copyright":"© Jackal Pan/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=bald+cypress&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261104_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261104_AutumnChina"},"Ssd":"20261104","Name":"AutumnChina","Market":"ROW","Hash":"6919148725","FullDateString":"4 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"On Brazil's southern coast, Taquaras Beach offers a quieter escape in Balneário Camboriú, Santa Catarina. Clear blue-green waters meet a broad stretch of golden sand, backed by lush vegetation and rolling green hills. Away from the livelier atmosphere of the city centre, the beach is known for its peaceful surroundings and natural beauty. With its inviting shoreline, rich greenery and unspoilt feel, Taquaras showcases a calmer side of this popular Brazilian coastal destination.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Camburiu_ROW3589076688_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Camburiu_ROW3589076688_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Taquaras Beach, Balneário Camboriú, Brazil","Copyright":"© MaRabelo/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261103_Camburiu\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Balne%c3%a1rio+Cambori%c3%ba&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261103_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261103_Camburiu"},"Ssd":"20261103","Name":"Camburiu","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3589076688","FullDateString":"3 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"These polar bears are gathering along the shores of Hudson Bay in Manitoba, Canada, waiting for sea ice to form so they can head back out to hunt seals. Polar bears are powerful swimmers, expert hunters and remarkably adapted to life in one of Earth's harshest environments. Yet shrinking sea ice means many spend longer on land, making it harder to find food and raising the risk of encounters with people.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_ROW5956466149_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.HudsonBear_ROW5956466149_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Polar bear and cubs by Hudson Bay, Manitoba, Canada","Copyright":"© Danita Delimont/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Polar+bear&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261102_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261102_HudsonBear"},"Ssd":"20261102","Name":"HudsonBear","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5956466149","FullDateString":"2 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today we're enjoying the misty views sweeping across the Black Forest, which stretches for around 160 kilometres across south-west Germany, bringing together wooded hills, deep valleys, lakes and charming towns. Its highest point, Feldberg, rises to 1,493 metres, while the Black Forest is also the starting point for the Danube and Neckar rivers. There's plenty of history and tradition here too. Forestry has long played an important role in the region, while its centuries-old clockmaking heritage helped make the distinctive cuckoo clock famous far beyond Germany.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_ROW3364796116_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SchwarzwaldAutumn_ROW3364796116_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Black Forest, Baden-Württemberg, Germany","Copyright":"© Britus/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Black+Forest+Germany&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261101_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261101_SchwarzwaldAutumn"},"Ssd":"20261101","Name":"SchwarzwaldAutumn","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3364796116","FullDateString":"1 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Lake Braies sits almost 1,500 metres above sea level in the Dolomites of South Tyrol, northern Italy. Surrounded by forest and the dramatic peaks of the Fanes-Sennes-Braies Nature Park, the lake is known for its striking green and blue waters. A 3.5-kilometre trail circles the shore, while traditional wooden rowing boats offer another way to take in the scenery. The lake is also a starting point for several mountain walks, including the Dolomites' famous Alta Via 1.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_ROW3051494546_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AlpineBraies_ROW3051494546_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Lake Braies, Fanes‑Sennes‑Braies Nature Park, Dolomites, Italy","Copyright":"© leonid_tit/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261031_AlpineBraies\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Braies+Dolomites&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261031_0700\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261031_AlpineBraies"},"Ssd":"20261031","Name":"AlpineBraies","Market":"ROW","Hash":"3051494546","FullDateString":"31 Oct 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Dawn's first light is reflected on the frozen surface of Abraham Lake, framed by Rocky Mountains peaks in western Canada. In winter, this picturesque lake in Alberta is famous for its frozen bubbles of methane gas, trapped beneath the ice. Strong winds keep the surface clear of snow, offering winter-long views. Come spring, when the ice thaws, the gas escapes into the atmosphere.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.AbrahamCanada_ROW4975668347_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.AbrahamCanada_ROW4975668347_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Abraham Lake in Alberta, Canada","Copyright":"© Guang Cao/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261113_AbrahamCanada\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Abraham+Lake+Alberta&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261113_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261113_AbrahamCanada"},"Ssd":"20261113","Name":"AbrahamCanada","Market":"ROW","Hash":"4975668347","FullDateString":"13 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Just north of Moab, Utah, the high-desert park is home to more than 2,000 natural sandstone arches—the densest concentration of arches in the world. Today's image, North Window, is one of the best-known formations in the park's Windows Section, where towering fins, openings and sculpted sandstone create a landscape that looks almost architectural.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_ROW5709754561_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.NorthWindow_ROW5709754561_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"North Window, Arches National Park, Moab, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© lightphoto/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Arches+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261112_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261112_NorthWindow"},"Ssd":"20261112","Name":"NorthWindow","Market":"ROW","Hash":"5709754561","FullDateString":"12 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Atlantic Forest is one of the world's great biodiversity hotspots, stretching along much of Brazil's Atlantic coast and into Argentina and Paraguay. Its landscape includes tropical and subtropical forests, mangroves and coastal habitats, providing a home for around 20,000 plant species and an extraordinary variety of wildlife, including jaguars and golden lion tamarins. Much of the forest has disappeared over the centuries, but it continues to play an important role in storing carbon and providing fresh water for millions of people across the region.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_ROW8494593651_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.Atlantica_ROW8494593651_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"The Atlantic Forest, Brazil","Copyright":"© FG Trade/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Atlantic+Forest+Brazil&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261111_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261111_Atlantica"},"Ssd":"20261111","Name":"Atlantica","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8494593651","FullDateString":"11 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"From above, Rose Island looks like a brushstroke of green surrounded by every shade of blue. Just five kilometres east of Paradise Island in The Bahamas, this slender cay trades busy roads and city blocks for sandy shores, shallow waters and an inland lagoon. Its peaceful appearance comes with a touch of movie drama. Rose Island was used as a filming location for the 1965 James Bond adventure 'Thunderball', including the explosive destruction of the Disco Volante.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_ROW8217613794_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RoseIsland_ROW8217613794_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Aerial view of Rose Island, The Bahamas","Copyright":"© Abstract Aerial Art/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rose+Island+Bahamas&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261110_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261110_RoseIsland"},"Ssd":"20261110","Name":"RoseIsland","Market":"ROW","Hash":"8217613794","FullDateString":"10 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Cross the Guadalquivir River in Seville, the capital of Spain's Andalusia region, and the city's rhythm seems to change. On the other side lies Triana, a colourful neighbourhood where ceramics, flamenco and local traditions are woven into everyday life. Since the 19th century, the Isabel II Bridge, also known as the Triana Bridge, has connected the neighbourhood to Seville's historic centre.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_ROW7617415595_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.TrianaSpain_ROW7617415595_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Historic district of Triana, Seville, Spain","Copyright":"© Andrzej Rostek/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Seville+Spain&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261109_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261109_TrianaSpain"},"Ssd":"20261109","Name":"TrianaSpain","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7617415595","FullDateString":"9 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The Ebro Delta in Catalonia is one of Spain's most rewarding places to see flamingos. These unmistakable birds can be spotted throughout the year, often gathering in the delta's shallow lagoons, salt pans and coastal waters. Their long legs let them wade through the water while feeding, while their pink colouring comes from pigments found in their diet. With wetlands, rice fields, beaches and the Mediterranean all meeting here, the delta provides an important home for both resident and migratory birds. Flamingos have become one of its most recognisable sights, adding a splash of colour to this remarkable landscape.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DeltaEbro_ROW7248981899_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DeltaEbro_ROW7248981899_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"Flamingos in Ebro Delta Natural Park, Catalonia, Spain","Copyright":"© mafrmcfa/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261108_DeltaEbro\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ebro+Delta+Natural+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261108_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261108_DeltaEbro"},"Ssd":"20261108","Name":"DeltaEbro","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7248981899","FullDateString":"8 Nov 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Bison are among the largest land mammals in the world, capable of weighing up to 900 kilograms and reaching speeds of 65 kilometres per hour despite their massive size. Despite often being called a buffalo, the American bison is not one of the true buffaloes, which are native to Africa and Asia. Its scientific name, Bison bison, leaves little room for confusion.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_ROW7172064410_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.DakotaBison_ROW7172064410_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Info","Title":"A bison in the grasslands of Theodore Roosevelt National Park, North Dakota, USA","Copyright":"© Tandem Stock/Adobe Stock","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261107_DakotaBison\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=American+bison&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261107_0800\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261107_DakotaBison"},"Ssd":"20261107","Name":"DakotaBison","Market":"ROW","Hash":"7172064410